{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Abraham was to become etc.</b> — meaning: I need to inform him of the merit of the righteous, that they will deliver themselves and the people of their city, contrary to what He thought and as we have written nearby. And that is His saying <b>he will become a great nation and all the nations of the earth will be blessed through him</b> — that they will intercede on their behalf, and the word ״through him״ refers back to ״great nation.״" "And if you say: what does this disclosure avail for the nation that comes after him? — for this He said <b>For I have known him, in order that he may charge</b> etc., meaning: HaShem knew Abraham, that he would strive with his children to do good; therefore He informs him, in order that he may charge his children and make known to them the deeds of the Blessed One, and through this <b>they will keep the way of HaShem</b>." "And His saying <b>in order that HaShem may bring upon Abraham</b> — here He made known that the essential love is not for Abraham's seed, but the love of Abraham himself is the essence, and all the thoughts of the Holy One, blessed be He, are to bring upon Abraham that which He spoke, to do good to him and to his seed forever. For if they do not keep the way of HaShem, the Benefactor will find no way to fulfill His promises to His beloved, to do good to his children."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "In this comment, למען אשר יצוה and ושמרו דרך ה׳ are drawn from the following verse (Genesis 18:19); the Or HaChaim quotes them here but the lemma address remains 18:18."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:06.562194480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}